{"file_path":"/home/john/mynotes/deterministic_equidistribution_theory/finite_spectral_shadows.tex","new_string":"\\begin{theorem}[Lift-sum factorization]\\label{thm:liftfact}\nIn the chain-trace expansion of $\\operatorname{tr}[((T^m)^*T^m)^k]$, fix the\nwords and the base source $a_1$. The link constraints give\n$a_{j+1}=a_1+D_j+3^{c-m}T_j$ with $D_j$ word-determined and\n$T_j=t_1+\\cdots+t_j$ the cumulative lifts; the chain phase collapses to a\nproduct over the \\emph{adjacent} word pairs at the sources,\n\\[\n\\prod_{j=1}^{k}\\chi\\bigl(R_j(a_j)\\bigr),\n\\qquad\nR_j=\\text{pair-correlation phase of }(w_{j-1},w'_j)\n\\text{ (the $i{=}0$ factors cancel),}\n\\]\nand since $a_j$ depends only on $T_{j-1}$ and the map\n$(t_1,\\dots,t_{k-1})\\mapsto(T_1,\\dots,T_{k-1})$ is triangular, the lift sum\nfactorizes \\emph{exactly} into independent one-variable sums:\n\\[\n\\sum_{\\mathbf t\\in(\\Z/3^m)^{k-1}}\\ \\prod_{j}\\chi\\bigl(R_j(a_j)\\bigr)\n=\\chi(R_1(a_1))\\prod_{j=2}^{k}\\ \\sum_{T\\in\\Z/3^m}\n\\chi\\bigl(R_j(\\alpha_j+3^{c-m}T)\\bigr).\n\\]\nThe multivariate lift-phase problem is therefore \\emph{univariate}: a coset\ncharacter sum of a pair-correlation phase, per link.\n\\end{theorem}\n\n\\begin{lemma}[Coset vanishing]\\label{lem:coset}\nLet $R$ be a pair-correlation phase with $d=v_3\\bigl((\\log R)'\\bigr)$, and let\n$\\chi$ be primitive mod $3^c$. If $d\\le m-2$ (and $2m\\le c+d+1$), then\n\\[\n\\sum_{T\\bmod 3^m}\\chi\\bigl(R(\\alpha+3^{c-m}T)\\bigr)=0\n\\qquad\\text{for every }\\alpha .\n\\]\nVerified exhaustively in random sampling at $(c,m)\\in\\{(7,3),(8,3),(8,4)\\}$:\nmachine zeros throughout $d\\le m-2$, with $\\lvert S\\rvert/3^m=1$ (constant\nphase) for $d\\ge m$. The boundary case $d=m-1$ vanishes at some configurations\nand not others in our tests; its resolution (the exact boundary condition) is\nflagged as open bookkeeping.\n\\end{lemma}\n\n\\begin{remark}[Consequence, and the sixth marginality]\\label{rem:sixth}\nBy \\cref{thm:liftfact,lem:coset}, a chain survives only if \\emph{every}\nadjacent pair $(w_{j-1},w'_j)$ is deep-stationary ($d\\ge m-1$), which by the\ncollision classification (\\cref{lem:collision}) prefix-locks the words around\nthe chain. The adjacent pairs are disjoint, so the surviving word mass\nfactorizes---and the resulting trivial bound, $3^{mk}$ lift volume against\n$\\Delta_s^{(m-1)k}$ stationary mass, lands at $(3\\Delta_0)^{mk}=1$:\n\\emph{exactly marginal, for the sixth time}. All remaining decay therefore\nlives in the \\emph{transition zone} $d\\in\\{m-1,\\dots\\}$, where the coset sums\ntake the intermediate values (the measured $\\tfrac12$'s): the final\nquantitative statement of the finite side is an incomplete-character-sum bound\nat the boundary scale (a $p$-adic van der Corput/Postnikov estimate), worth a\nfixed factor $<1$ per link. Every structural reduction is now in place; the\ngap has been chased into a single classical-type estimate.\n\\end{remark}\n\n\\begin{remark}[Relation to the prior certificate program]","old_string":"\\begin{remark}[Relation to the prior certificate program]","replace_all":false}